  "notes": "FORMS:\n{外|がい} (outside) + {泊|はく} (staying overnight) → staying overnight outside\n{外泊|がいはく}する (to stay out overnight)\n\nUSAGE:\n- Student dormitories often require {外泊|がいはく}{届|とどけ} (overnight absence notification)\n- Hospitals may allow {外泊|がいはく} for patients who are recovering well\n- Sometimes used when discussing where someone spent the night\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {泊|と}まる (to stay overnight)\n- {宿泊|しゅくはく} (lodging, staying at an inn)\n- {朝帰|あさがえ}り (coming home in the morning after staying out)",
